.TH unexpand 1 (date) "GNU coreutils (unreleased)"
.SH NAME
unexpand \- convert spaces to tabs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY unexpand
.RI [ OPTION \~.\|.\|.\&]
.RI [ FILE \~.\|.\|.\&]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" Add any additional description here
.PP
Convert blanks in each FILE to tabs, writing to standard output.
.PP
With no FILE, or when FILE is \-, read standard input.
.PP
Mandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#unexpand\-a
\fB\-a, \-\-all\fP
.UE
convert all blanks, instead of just initial blanks
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#unexpand\-\-first\-only
\fB\-\-first\-only\fP
.UE
convert only leading sequences of blanks (overrides \fB\-a\fR)
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#unexpand\-t
\fB\-t, \-\-tabs=\,N\fP
.UE
have tabs N characters apart instead of 8 (enables \fB\-a\fR)
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#unexpand\-t
\fB\-t, \-\-tabs=\,LIST\fP
.UE
use comma separated list of tab positions.
The last specified position can be prefixed with '/'
to specify a tab size to use after the last
explicitly specified tab stop.  Also a prefix of '+'
can be used to align remaining tab stops relative to
the last specified tab stop instead of the first column
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/unexpand#unexpand\-\-help
\fB\-\-help\fP
.UE
display this help and exit
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/unexpand#unexpand\-\-version
\fB\-\-version\fP
.UE
output version information and exit
